To configure Decision Center (DC) to look for the SSP on a different application server, you need to implement your own SSP resolver. 

Here's how you can do it:

1. Create your own SSP resolver class that implements the `IlrSSPResolver` interface.
2. In this class, implement the `getSSPURL` method, which will return the URL of the SSP service.
3. In this method, you can use the server name to determine which SSP URL to return. For example, you can have two servers defined in RTS: `testingServer1` and `testingServer2`, each with its own SSP URL.
4. In the `getSSPURL` method, you can use the server name to return the correct SSP URL. For example:
```java
if (serverName.equals("testingServer1")) {
    return new URL("http://server1:9000/testing/sspService");
} else if (serverName.equals("testingServer2")) {
    return new URL("http://server2:9000/testing/sspService");
} else {
    return new URL("http://server1:9000/testing/sspService");
}
```
5. Once you have implemented your own SSP resolver, add it to the `teamserver.war` file.
6. Set the `teamserver.defaultSSPResolver.class` property to your custom SSP resolver class.
7. Restart the application server.

By implementing your own SSP resolver, you can configure DC to look for the SSP on a different application server.

